rva23 run notes

the docs from ch, that don't fully work: https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/cloud-hypervisor/blob/main/docs/riscv.md


our install docs:

1) setup a ubuntu 24.04.02 qemu rva23 sim (ask lea for details), make sure it has kvm enabled.
2) run the native_compile/setup.sh file
3) cargo build doesnt work due to failing tests. run `cargo build --bin cloud-hypervisor`
4) this build took about 20-30 minutes on our hardware. i heavily recommend setting up mold and sccache to make it faster after first attempt.
5) then run the compiled binary
6) I (caleb/hero) am using odorobo to run the binary in a debug state, but using it directly and connecting over socket is likely better for debugging.
7) the code for creating vms in odorobo does work so you should be able use it as a reference for that. its in odorobo-agent/src/state


unfortunately running the binary currently doesnt work due to panic in hypervisor/src/kvm/mod.rs L1151, which runs Kvm::new().
This is likely due to unsafe code inside of the kvm bindings, but I haven't been able to figure it out due to some weird issue with backtraces.
Should work on it within the next few days at worst (4/15)


there is also cross_compile but it doesnt work due to issues with openssl rva23 cross compilation.
it is written for fedora (or fedora based distros).
if you can figure out how to make openssl work that would be good too.
